      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the late 19th and early 20th centuries, Magnolia Avenue grew as a railroad‑linked transportation and commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dallas.wiki/a/Magnolia_Avenue_(Fort_Worth)",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After mid‑century decline, revitalization since the 1990s restored historic buildings and sparked a vibrant arts scene.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dallas.wiki/a/Magnolia_Avenue_(Fort_Worth)",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Magnolia Avenue now serves as a cultural corridor, hosting eclectic restaurants, bars, art galleries, and live music venues.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
